   "issue": "`exists_partition_stepGraphonAvg_ne_bernoulliMeasure` proves `\u2203 P W, P.parts = {{0},{1},{2}} \u2227 stepGraphonAvg P hP W \u2260 W`. Per the naming dictionary, `ne` is followed by the right-hand side of `\u2260`, so the name states `stepGraphonAvg \u2026 \u2260 bernoulliMeasure \u2026` \u2014 a graphon compared to a measure. Every other `_bernoulliMeasure` name in the repo has the measure as the actual object of the head relation (`binomial_one_eq_bernoulliMeasure`, `integral_bernoulliMeasure`, `pgf_bernoulliMeasure`), so the suffix is read as the RHS here, not as a carrier qualifier. The right-hand side is in fact `W` itself.",
